Test SSTV fixtures (go/internal/decode/testdata/sstv_*.wav,
tests/data/ref_sstv.wav) are generated by tools/gen_sstv_fixtures.py using
pysstv, an independent SSTV encoder:

  pysstv — https://github.com/dnet/pysstv
  Copyright (c) 2014-2022 Andras Veres-Szentkiralyi
  License: GNU General Public License v3.0

pysstv is a test-time fixture generator only; no pysstv code is compiled
into sdrstream. The Go decoder implements the Martin / Scottie / Robot 36
line schedules from the published mode specifications (G3OQD Martin
modes, GM3SBC Scottie modes, Robot Research Robot 36), cross-checked
against the QSSTV mode table (src/sstv/sstvparam.cpp, GPL) and
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slow-scan_television .
